! ax4b_2a_rhw_fullword.strap -- jb_ax4b "I-BOX 4", routine 148 (1248,
! "INDEX MODIFICATION TEST", banner PDF p.113: "TEST2. CHECK FULL WORD
! MODIFICATION IN BOTH LEFT AND RIGHT HALF OF THE INSTRUCTION."), TEST
! 2A "CHECK RIGHT HALF WORD MODIFICATION OF FULL WD. INST.":
!
!   PDF p.125  010047.00-010103.00  I4817 gate, I4817A, I4818: bits 32-34
!   PDF p.126  010103.40-010137.00  bits 35, 36, exit, I4819: bits 37, 38
!   PDF p.127  010137.40-010175.40  bits 39-41, exit, I4820: bits 42, 43
!   PDF p.128  010176.00-010201.00  the end of the bit-43 block
!   PDF p.129  010201.40-010227.00  bits 44-46, exit
!   PDF p.130  010227.40-010263.00  I4821: bits 47-50, exit
!   PDF p.153  011356.00-011360.00  148K29-148K31; 011372.00 148ER1
!   PDF p.190  013035.00            1000 ("INDX WD. OF ONES.")
!   PDF p.191  013054.00-013113.00  BIT0-BIT18, BIT23-BIT25, BIT27, BIT31
!   PDF p.192  013123.00, 013143.00 BIT39, BIT55
!
! No printed page numbers on these sheets: cited by PDF page and octal
! location.  Read from the page images at 150 dpi; checked row for row
! against the printed machine code by
! tests/verify_ax4b_2a_rhw_fullword_listing.py.
!
! WHAT IT TESTS (IBM's code, unchanged).  A full-word VFL load whose
! SECOND-half I field is 1 ("... 51"): X1's value modifies the length,
! byte size and offset of the instruction.  For k = 0..18, X1 := BITk
! (one value bit), which IBM names "INDEX BIT 32+k" -- the instruction
! bit it lands on:
!   k = 0-2 (bits 32-34)  "NO CHANGE TO INSTRUCTION": L(BU),BIT0,($X1)
!                         must still load BIT0 whole (KV BIT0 / BXE)
!   k = 3-8 (bits 35-40)  the length, 0 (= 64) + 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1:
!                         "BECOMES BU 32, 8" ... "BU, 1, 8", checked as
!                         the count or refill of the $R word against a
!                         pair of BIT constants (KC/KV, BXH then BXL),
!                         or for length 1 KV BIT17 / BXE
!   k = 9-11 (bits 41-43) the byte size of L(B,64,8),148K29..31: "BECOMES
!                         B,64,4" / 2 / 1 -- the sign byte's width, so
!                         148K29 (37), 148K30 (7), 148K31 (3) load as +1
!                         (KV BIT17: the refill is 1)
!   k = 12-18 (bits 44-50) the offset, 0 + 64, 32, ... 1, of
!                         L(BU),BITn,($X1) with n - offset = 23: the
!                         loaded bit must land in bit 23 (KV BIT23 /
!                         BXE, from $L for offset 64, else $R)
! Reference Manual printed p.21 (PDF 24), quoted in StretchExecute.bsv's
! vflSecondIndex: "bit position 3 of the index word is aligned with bit
! position 35 of the instruction; the three high-order bits of the
! index word are ignored" -- which is why bits 32-34 change nothing.
!
! The gate at I4817 refuses to run if 148ER1's value (TEST 1A's error
! store) is nonzero, or (I4817A) if its refill (TEST 1C's) is nonzero;
! 148ER1 is 0 here, so it falls through to I4818.  The count (TEST 1B's)
! is not looked at.  "B,I50" and "B,I4822" leave the test; neither runs.
!
! FOUR SEGMENTS, each ending in "B,SSW": I4817 + I4818 (bits 32-36),
! I4819 (37-41), I4820 (42-46), I4821 (47-50).  The driver runs this
! deck four times: from END (I4817) and with ENTRY=I4819, I4820, I4821
! (gen_tb.py).  Continuity rows after each B,SSW are never run.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS (not on these pages):
!   * SSIP's entry points: SSW (001301.00) is a PASS halt, SERS
!     (001304.00) a FAIL halt, SEN/SENO (001310.00/001311.00) data words
!     SIC stores into.  The addresses are the listing's own (B,SSW
!     prints "1301.10 00", B,SERS "1304.10 00", SIC,SEN "1310.00 80",
!     SIC,SENO+.32 "1311.40 80"); the contents are SSIP's, which is not
!     transcribed.  SIC "is executed if and only if the associated
!     branching is successful" (Reference Manual printed p.41, PDF 44),
!     so SEN stays 0 on a pass and names the error entry on a failure.
!   * IC248, I4822 (TEST 2B's entry, 010264.00) and I50 (routine 150,
!     011424.00) are SYN'd from the printed "LX,$X13,IC248" (11306.32
!     10), "B,I4822" (10264.10 00) and "B,I50" (11424.10 00).
!   * Notation only: the page's "%" and the box glyph are "(" and ")";
!     the label glyph the scan shows as "1" is the letter I (I48..,
!     I000), as for every ax4b label (docs/listing_typography.md).
!     Nothing else changed.
!
! RESULT, 2026-11-19: every segment halts at SSW (PASS, PC 1410) with
! SEN = 0.  The driver compares PC, SEN, CYCLES and the pins listed in
! tests/run_tests.sh; CYCLES is MODEL BEHAVIOUR, not IBM's timing.
! SEN, on a failure, is SIC's link: the half-word after the "B,SERS" that
! was taken, so it names the failing check.
! MODEL INJECTIONS, OBSERVED (each built in its own scratch copy of
! stretch/bsv/, all 19 segment runs of TESTs 1-2 repeated; the
! worktree's bsv/ was never edited):
!   second-half I dropped (vflSecondIndex returns the field unchanged)
!     -> all four segments FAIL halt: I4817 SEN 010111.40 (the first
!     length check, KC BIT4/BIT3), CYCLES 611; I4819 SEN 010131.40,
!     CYCLES 208; I4820 SEN 010173.40, CYCLES 185; I4821 SEN 010235.40,
!     CYCLES 182.
!   the index field misaligned by three bits (d = x.addr[23:8] instead
!     of [20:5]: index bit 0 lands on instruction bit 35, bits 16-18 are
!     dropped) -> I4817 FAIL halt, SEN 010067.40: the bit-32 "NO CHANGE"
!     check (KV BIT0), CYCLES 265; I4819 010131.40, I4820 010173.40,
!     I4821 010235.40, as above.
!   VFL accumulator offset forced to 0 -> I4820 FAIL halt, SEN 010207.40,
!     CYCLES 415; I4821 SEN 010235.40, CYCLES 182; I4817, I4819 PASS.
!   byte size always 8 (effByteSize ignores BS) -> I4819 FAIL halt, SEN
!     010161.40 (the BS checks, 148K29-31), CYCLES 699; I4820 SEN
!     010173.40, CYCLES 185; I4817, I4821 PASS.
!   CONTROL: the unmodified model in the same scratch arrangement: all
!     19 runs PASS with the pins in run_tests.sh.
!
! ---- SSIP's entry points: SUBSTITUTES (not on these pages) -----------
        SLC, (8)1301.0
SSW     BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: PASS (the return to SSIP)
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $                        ! SUBSTITUTE: FAIL (SSIP's error report)
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's error link word
SENO    DD(BU,64,8), 0                ! SUBSTITUTE: SIC's other link word
!
! IC248, I4822, I50: SYN from the printed rows that name them.
IC248   SYN, (8)11306.0
I4822   SYN, (8)10264.0
I50     SYN, (8)11424.0
!
        SLC, (8)10047.0
! ======================================================================
